From 3f03ced2a3f415ea22d8277077529ce85d02c52a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Hilton <robert.a.hilton.jr@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 22:54:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] eeschema: expose SyncSelection cross-probing to IPC API
 clients

API clients (plugins) had no way to make the schematic editor show a
symbol: eeschema registers no selection handlers in 10.0, and RunAction
is unhandled. Master gained a SyncSelection command for this in the
cross-probe API rework; this brings that command to 10.0 in the
smallest form that reuses what eeschema already has.

The MAIL_SELECTION_FORCE body in KiwayMailIn is lifted into a public
SCH_EDIT_FRAME::SyncSelectionFromSpec(), so the API handler and the
PCB editor's cross-probe drive one implementation: findItemsFromSync-
Selection, SCH_SELECTION_TOOL::SyncSelection (sheet switch, select,
centre/zoom per preferences) and the selection flash. The handler
turns the request's SelectionSpecs into the existing sync-string form
(F<ref>, P<ref>/<pin>) and honours the on_selection preference for
implicit contexts exactly as master does. The proto file is master's,
unchanged, so clients written against master work here as-is.
